1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:05,648
QoreStamp is a post-quantum receipt you can stamp and verify on the QoreChain testnet.

2
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:09,266
A lunch I.O.U. in a chat can be denied later.

3
00:00:09,216 --> 00:00:13,347
After Q-Day, a classical signature alone may not be enough either.

4
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,456
Write the memo.

5
00:00:15,406 --> 00:00:19,012
QoreStamp shows its SHA two fifty six digest.

6
00:00:19,012 --> 00:00:21,143
The chain stores only that hash.

7
00:00:21,143 --> 00:00:23,591
Anyone with the original text can check it.

8
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:36,141
On QoreChain, opening the EVM window is signed twice: once with secp two five six k one, and once with ML-DSA eighty seven, the FIPS two zero four post-quantum key.

9
00:00:36,976 --> 00:00:41,436
Stamp Registry then records the digest, the stamper, and the time.

10
00:00:41,386 --> 00:00:46,136
Six local tests cover the contract, including a zero digest rejection.

11
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:49,049
Paste the transaction hash.

12
00:00:48,999 --> 00:00:58,131
The public testnet A.P.I. must show success, a P.Q.C. Hybrid Signature, and a pqc hybrid verify event with status verified.

13
00:00:59,012 --> 00:01:00,143
QoreStamp.

14
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:02,935
Built for Build Before Q-Day, Quantum Pass.

15
00:01:02,935 --> 00:01:04,185
Testnet only.

16
00:01:04,185 --> 00:01:06,777
No camera, no mainnet funds.

